  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="KTHORLAQ&apos;S HONOUR (1)" id="f0b8-f22c-622b-023f" hidden="false">
      <description>This ability may be used any time a SALAMANDER model fails a Fallback Check. The model automatically passes the test. It may be used more than once in a Round.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="FLAMES OF KTHORLAQ (1)" id="ae06-a1c5-957a-754b" hidden="false">
      <description>Select a SALAMANDER model in the warband. The model gains Bloodlust and Smash until the end of the current Round.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Spell - Shimmer" id="d174-58ff-d98b-2f27" hidden="false">
      <description>Enemy models targeting friendly models that are within 9” of the caster suffer a -1 modifier to hit with all attacks. This lasts until the end of the Round. Place a spell effect marker on the casting model as a reminder.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="LEAP OF DEATH (1)" id="8b66-2b73-1c95-59cc" hidden="false">
      <description>Use this ability when declaring a Run action with this model that does not Engage. This model gains the Fly special rule until the end of the Turn. At the end of this Run, this model may make a free Ranged attack: Range 6”, Breath, Piercing (1), from each of its front and rear base edges.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="GUN SMOKE (1)" id="74ed-1e07-5ea2-71eb" hidden="false">
      <description>Use this ability when this model attacks with a pistol, before dice are rolled. This model gains the Stealthy and Dodge special rules until the end of the Round, regardless of whether the attack hits.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Blazing Brands" id="a7aa-6bbd-9d27-6f54" hidden="false">
      <description>While Firebrand is part of the same warband, this model has the Stubborn special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="RAPID FIRE (2)" id="dfb2-52f2-75ef-9a99" hidden="false">
      <description>Use this ability when this model is aboutto perform a ranged attack,before dice are rolled. The model may shoot twice at two different targets that are within3” of each other following the normal targeting rules. This cannot be as part of a Group or Fatigue Action.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Riposte" id="0192-ff68-06dc-c8f2" hidden="false">
      <description>When thismodel is the target of a Melee attackand alltheattacker’sdice miss, this model may make a Retaliation for free. No Activated or Fatigued counter is placed on this model after a Riposte.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fancy Swordplay" id="94bd-cfc3-53b9-b61a" hidden="false">
      <description>Melee attacks against this model are made with a -1 modifier to the attackers Me stat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Salamander Legend" id="1131-ad33-a947-c46b" hidden="false">
      <description>When taken in a Salamander warband, Firebrand is not considered a Mercenary. She does count as being at Rank 5 to match her legendary status however.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Weapon - Two-handed Weapon" id="28c2-80b7-60dc-49e8" hidden="false">
      <description>Melee type equipment. The model gains an additional Crushing Strength (taking it to 2), but increases its Armor by 1 (i.e 5+ becomes 6+).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="INNER FIRE (2)" id="0bce-0fe3-2d49-6bfd" hidden="false">
      <description>Use this ability when this model activates. The model’s Armour improves by 2 until the end
of the Round (i.e. 6+ becomes 4+) to no better than 3+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Attack - Elemental Fire" id="2c68-64eb-43e1-eedb" hidden="false">
      <description>This model may make a Ranged attack with a Shoot action using Elemental Fire. Range 9”, 3D8, Breath. The attack always hits on a 5+ regardless of any modifiers.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="NATURE&apos;S INFERNO (2)" id="d242-3681-db0e-f4eb" hidden="false">
      <description>Use this ability when this model makes a Ranged Attack with Elemental Fire before any dice are rolled. The attack has Piercing (1).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="ORDEAL OF FIRE (2)" id="d7ce-eaee-28a9-c98f" hidden="false">
      <description>Use this ability during this model’s activation, before or after an action, even if it is Engaged or Knocked-down. Models of race SALAMANDER (including the Veteran itself) and Fire Elementals are immune to the effects of this attack. All other models within 2” take 2 automatic hits with Piercing (1). Make Armour rolls as normal. This ability can only be used once per game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="HEALING FLAME (2)" id="496a-d729-dd3c-71b4" hidden="false">
      <description>Spend the Power as a long action. Roll a die for each friendly model within 6”. On score of 6+, that model regains a wound previously suffered.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Elemental Fuel" id="34d6-4f22-1438-3f01" hidden="false">
      <description>While within 6” of one or more friendly Fire Elementals, this model’s Special Abilities cost 1 less Power to use.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="SHIFTING SCALES (1)" id="f6b6-b024-a559-f35a" hidden="false">
      <description>Use this ability when this model activates. Until the end of the Round, the models gains the Dodge and Parry abilities.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rekindle the Embers" id="3429-95d3-0f47-64ca" hidden="false">
      <description>While within 6” of a friendly Fire Elemental or Mage Priest, this model has the Bloodlust special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Brothers in Arms" id="0007-21d3-a56c-c645" hidden="false">
      <description>This model gains +1 die in Melee while it is a member of a Shield Wall group action.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Inspiring (Ghekkotah only)" id="a8e2-751f-d827-31c6" hidden="false">
      <description>A model with this rule, and all friendly models within 6” of it, may re-roll failed Nerve tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="SAVAGE ROAR (2)" id="b1b5-6d5e-afc2-8228" hidden="false">
      <description>Use Savage Roar when the Tyrant is the target of a Melee attack, before the attack roll is made. The attacking model reduces its Crushing Strength by 1, to a minimum of 0 for that attack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Simmering Rage" id="209b-acdf-a3de-0bfd" hidden="false">
      <description>For each wound the Tyrant has suffered, increase the Tyrant’s Crushing Strength by +1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="SAVAGE IMPACT (1)" id="1baa-9789-1981-1923" hidden="false">
      <description>Use before a qualifying Charge action. If any wounds are caused by this model in the subsequent free Melee attack and it is not killed, the target is also pushed directly backwards 3”, stopping if it hits any terrain, objectives or other models. The Rhinosaur Cataphract may then choose to move forwards back into base contact to remain Engaged.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="SHIELD WALL (2)" id="c942-73e9-36a5-d5ff" hidden="false">
      <description>Group Action. This works exactly like the standard Group Assault, but this model must be the group leader, and the group members can only consist of COMMAND, WARRIOR and SUPPORT models. In addition, enemy models retaliating against Melee attacks from this Group Assault, suffer a -2 to-hit modifier.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="SLAMBACK (1)" id="4a69-6bb9-8169-f08d" hidden="false">
      <description>Use this ability when this model declares a Retaliation before dice arerolled. Any hits this Retaliation scores are resolved with an additional+1 Crushing Strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="EVASIVE MANOUVRES (2)" id="48ba-36be-ba96-ecb5" hidden="false">
      <description>Group Action:
What: The group members each make a Run action with +1 Sp and gain theDodge special rule until the end of the Round. Group members can only be of classes COMMAND, WARRIOR or GRUNT. The Run cannot be used to Engage enemy models. All group membersmust finish their movement within 6” of each other.
When: Spend the Power to nominate this model as the group leader and the group and activate them together.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
